From 3a333ea2afd651220a7a12a076db8d9a87d03188 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Damien Thenot <damien.thenot@vates.tech>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:00:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(linstor): cache COW image info in the LINSTOR KV store

Scanning a LINSTOR SR calls `LinstorCowUtil.get_info` for every COW
volume, which costs a XAPI call plus a local or remote image read each
time. Store the image info used by the callers (hidden flag, virtual
size, parent uuid) in per-volume KV keys (`hidden`, `size-virt`,
`parent-uuid`) and serve `get_info` from them, reading the image only
when an entry is missing or invalid.

Read path:
- A hit needs the three fields valid and a cached parent that resolves
  to a volume. `sizePhys` and `sizeAllocated` are not cached (they
  change on guest writes), they are -1 when the info comes from the KV
  store.
- On a miss, the image is read. The fields that were valid in the KV
  store are compared with the image: every field that differs is
  logged, as a diagnostic only, and the image values are used.
- Only the master scans (SR scan and GC scan, `store_info=True`) write
  the info read on a miss: the master is the only writer.

Writers:
- Every `LinstorCowUtil` modifier goes through
  `_updating_volume_image_info`: the fields are invalidated before the
  image is modified and written after success, so a crash in between
  forces a re-read, never leaves stale values.
- `snapshot` reads the new image back: without `checkEmpty`, vhd-util
  skips an empty parent and links the new image to the grandparent.
- `force_repair` only invalidates, the next scan reads the image.
- `kill_data` and `force_coalesce` only modify data, they don't touch
  the info.
- `LinstorVDI._setHidden` in cleanup.py goes through `linstorcowutil`.
- Invalidation writes a marker instead of deleting the key: `linstor.KV`
  is a per-process snapshot, deleting a key unknown locally is not
  forwarded to LINSTOR.
- `update_volume_uuid` carries the keys to the new uuid. The children's
  cached parent is not rewritten: a renamed parent is a miss for them.
- The GC leaf-coalesce undo, the clone undo and the `DELETED_` renames
  invalidate the info of the volumes they rename.

Before a GC coalesce, `_checkCachedParentMatchesImage` reads the parent
from the image itself (never cached) and cancels the coalesce if it
isn't the parent of the tree: a stale cached parent would merge an
image into the wrong parent. The volume's cached info is then
invalidated, so the next scan reads the image and builds the right tree.

`linstor-kv-tool`: add `--remove-volume-image-info` and
`--remove-all-volumes-image-info` to force a re-read from the images.

Signed-off-by: Damien Thenot <damien.thenot@vates.tech>
